WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.030
- I always like to wrap
things up with something

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.500
that could bring you some extra cheer.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.713
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.370
So earlier this hour, we
met a teacher who taught

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.740
her second graders, how they
could make a real difference

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.603
in the community.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.101
Now I wanna talk to you about
another passionate teacher.

00:00:17.101 --> 00:00:19.184
This one is from right here in California

00:00:19.184 --> 00:00:21.584
and she's helping students
express themselves

00:00:21.584 --> 00:00:23.480
in her very first children's
book, let's say hi

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.530
to the author of Patty's Predicament.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.123
Vicky who watches on K F R E TV.

00:00:29.048 --> 00:00:30.062
Fresno. What's up

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:30.895
- Vicky.

00:00:30.895 --> 00:00:33.174
- Hi. How are you today?

00:00:33.174 --> 00:00:35.410
- I'm having a great day.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.353
I hope you are as well.

00:00:36.353 --> 00:00:38.492
Can you tell us about Patty's predicament?

00:00:38.492 --> 00:00:42.300
- Well, Kelly, in my 23
years as a classroom teacher,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.390
I found that there were
students that had avoidance

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.782
issues that weren't
getting their work done.

00:00:47.782 --> 00:00:50.193
And as a teacher, my
expectations are high.

00:00:50.193 --> 00:00:53.650
Those excuses are important
and I had empathy towards 'em

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.320
but we still need to get our work done.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.730
And I learned very quickly

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.300
that what was happening
outside the classroom

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.690
affects what happens inside the classroom.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.160
And so I was a seeker.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.190
I went out and I, are they hungry?

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.702
Do they have friends? What's
going on after school?

00:01:10.702 --> 00:01:12.840
Are they well?

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.440
And when I wrote this book,
this story is about a student

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.430
who's an amazing person in some ways.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.020
And in other ways she
has avoidance issues.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:25.040
And so Mrs. Becker, the
classroom teacher tries to

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.251
help Patty solve this predicament.

00:01:27.251 --> 00:01:28.680
- I love that.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.513
That's so true.

00:01:29.513 --> 00:01:31.070
My mom was a teacher and
it, and it's so true.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.750
Like what happens outside
the classroom definitely

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.640
affects emotionally where they're at.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.010
Like physically, if they're tired

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:38.210
like all those things come into play

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.292
but you say the book is
not just important for kids

00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:43.402
but for teachers as well to
maybe recognize that, right?

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.840
- Oh, absolutely.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:45.830
That's why really.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.190
That's why I wrote the
book when the pandemic hit

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:51.149
and I've always mentored
new teachers and it's like

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:53.740
oh my goodness, who's
gonna teach these teachers.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.690
They have to seek, they
have to break that code.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:02:00.050
And my sweet husband's like write a book.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.120
So I did.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.480
So I, my book is really, I
want every new teacher to have

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.100
in their hand, just, you know, be a seeker

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.152
figure it out that
child should not be left

00:02:09.152 --> 00:02:12.110
behind that child is so worthy

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.500
of your attention and your effort.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.160
- Absolutely. Ah, thank you so much, Vicky

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.930
for being an amazing
teacher, not only to students

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.320
but to other teachers too, you know

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.226
that's a club and you can
all help each other feed

00:02:24.226 --> 00:02:25.059
off of each other ideas.

00:02:25.059 --> 00:02:25.892
It's very, it's very cool.

00:02:25.892 --> 00:02:26.725
It's very

00:02:26.725 --> 00:02:28.715
teachers are the most
innovative people on the planet.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.395
Thank you so much for being a teacher.

00:02:30.395 --> 00:02:31.373
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.430
And that's not all, ma'am
our season long partner

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.804
pilot pen, makers of friction.

00:02:37.804 --> 00:02:39.350
The go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson show.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.320
Want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly, just

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.060
like you ma'am so they are
giving you a thousand dollars.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.572
How's that sound?

00:02:45.572 --> 00:02:47.410
(crowd cheering &amp; clapping)

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.139
- Wow. How amazing thank you so much.

00:02:50.139 --> 00:02:50.972
So unexpected.

00:02:50.972 --> 00:02:53.300
(cheering and clapping)

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.970
It's an honor to have you on this show.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:55.963
Thank you so much.

